== Land acknowledgement ==

Thunder Bay is on the traditional lands of the Anishinaabe peoples, including Fort William First Nation, within the Robinson-Superior Treaty territory, and is part of the historic Métis homeland. First Nations should have more say in, and more ownership of, how their traditional lands beyond their reserves are developed, including the land Thunder Bay stands on.

<small>The first sentence adapts the City of Thunder Bay's [https://www.thunderbay.ca/city-hall/indigenous-relations/deepening-understanding/ Deepening Understanding] page.</small>

The 378 addresses on Fort William First Nation reserve land wait until the Nation has answered our letter, and are left out if it has not answered within 30 days; see [[#Fort William First Nation|§ Fort William First Nation]].

== Summary ==

Human-reviewed import of '''missing civic address points''' from the City of Thunder Bay's municipal address layer. Each address is checked against a fresh OSM snapshot, so only addresses OSM does not already have are created. Every run is reviewed by a person in a local web UI before it is uploaded. Every upload is its own tagged changeset, and every decision is logged.

Thunder Bay's addresses in OSM today are almost entirely '''CanVec 6.0 interpolation''': 6,604 <code>addr:interpolation</code> ways (odd/even block ranges), whose endpoints are 12,763 of the 12,950 address nodes in the city (2026-11-06 Geofabrik extract). Apart from those there are about 190 standalone address nodes and 390 address-bearing ways. There are no import tags, no import page and little recent address activity; the last broad change was a 2018 retag.

'''Geographic scope:''' the City of Thunder Bay, Ontario, plus Fort William First Nation land in a separate phase. The City's 7 wards (Westfort, McIntyre, Neebing, Red River, Northwood, McKellar, Current River) split the work into review tiles.

Scope numbers (source snapshot #18, 2026-11-07):

{| class="wikitable"
! Rows !! Count !! Disposition
|-
| City of Thunder Bay (<code>CITY = THUNDER BAY</code>) || 44,722 || Candidates, phases 1–2.
|-
| Fort William First Nation (<code>CITY = FWFN</code>) || 378 || Phase 3, gated. 8 have no civic number and are dropped.
|-
| No <code>CITY</code> value || 2 || Reviewed by hand.
|-
! Total !! 45,102 !! Before conflation.
