Baseline conflation (2026-11-08) against the 2026-11-06 Geofabrik extract: 322 already in OSM, 27 near-matches for review, '''44,740 missing''' (44,379 in the City, 361 on Fort William First Nation land); 9 rows with no civic number are skipped. Only the missing ones are candidates for upload. The near-total gap is what the CanVec situation below predicts.

== Goals and non-goals ==

=== Goals ===
* Add the civic addresses OSM is missing in Thunder Bay, from the City's authoritative roster.
* Create no duplicates of addresses already in OSM, and change no existing address data.
* Keep a per-address audit trail (source row → verdict → reviewer decision → changeset → OSM id) anyone can inspect.

=== Non-goals ===
* '''No deletions''', '''no edits to existing objects''', '''no geometry edits''', '''no buildings''' and '''no <code>addr:interpolation</code> cleanup'''. Create-only, exactly as [[Toronto/Import/AddressPoints#Goals and non-goals|Toronto's]].
* '''The CanVec interpolation ways stay untouched during the import.''' Their cleanup is a separate, later effort; see [[#CanVec interpolation|§ CanVec interpolation]].

== Schedule ==

=== Contacts and reviewers ===
* '''Maintainer and first reviewer:''' toronto@comentality.com
* '''Local mappers contacted before this page went up:''' Matthew Darwin, eireidium. Both are invited to review.
* '''Fort William First Nation:''' Lands & Governance, by letter on 2026-11-08. See [[#Fort William First Nation|below]].
* '''Upload rule:''' nothing uploads without a reviewer's approval in the web UI.

=== Phases ===

Each phase can ship on its own and be reverted on its own.

* '''Phase 0 — community review.''' This page, a forum post tagged <code>import</code>, and a 14-day feedback window.
* '''Phase 1 — pilot, one tile.''' <code>mckellar-sw-sw-ne</code> in downtown Fort William: 495 candidates, 493 of them missing, fully reviewed by hand. One-week hold before Phase 2.
* '''Phase 2 — the City, ward by ward.''' One tile per changeset, 250–750 source addresses each, at most one changeset a minute by manual cadence.
* '''Phase 3 — Fort William First Nation.''' Only after the Nation has answered, or after the wait in [[#Fort William First Nation|§ Fort William First Nation]]. Its own tiles and changesets, never mixed with City tiles.
* '''Phase 4 — closeout and upkeep.''' A closing report here and on the forum thread. After that the City's new addresses are added monthly under the same rules, as for [[Toronto/Import/AddressPoints#Continuous maintenance|Toronto]].

== Fort William First Nation ==

The City's address layer includes 378 points on Fort William First Nation land, a separate jurisdiction from the City. They have no City parcel number. The City publishes them under the same open licence, so the licence permits importing them. But we must ask the Nation, since it is a separate jurisdiction. There is no Canadian OSM import precedent we could find either way.

* A letter went to FWFN Lands & Governance on 2026-11-08 asking: whether the Nation is comfortable with the addresses being in OSM; who assigns them; what the road the City lists as "Squaw Bay Road" is called today; and whether there is a process to follow.
* '''If the Nation says no''', Phase 3 does not happen, and this page says so.
* '''If the Nation asks for changes''' (names, spellings, a subset), we make them.
* '''If there is no reply''' after 30 days, we skip Phase 3.

== CanVec interpolation ==

Almost all of Thunder Bay's existing OSM addressing is CanVec block ranges: an odd and an even <code>addr:interpolation</code> way along each block face, with a numbered node at each end. The endpoints carry real-looking <code>addr:housenumber</code>/<code>addr:street</code> tags, but they are range limits placed along the road, not buildings. The ranges imply up to ~127,000 numbers for a city of ~45,000 addresses.

Like Toronto's, the engine does not count interpolation endpoints as existing addresses, so nearly every City address will be a candidate, and for a while the City's real points will sit alongside CanVec's synthetic ranges.

'''This import does not touch the interpolation ways or their endpoint nodes.''' Retiring them is a separate effort, done the way Toronto's was: [https://github.com/skfd/against-interpolation against-interpolation] generates one MapRoulette task per interpolation line once the City's points are in, showing the house numbers the City has for that block. A mapper checks them, then removes the line, keeping any endpoint that is part of a building or carries other tags. Lines with no City points on them get no task. That work is human-reviewed line by line and will get its own forum post before it starts.

== Import data ==

=== Source ===
* '''Dataset:''' Municipal Address layer, City of Thunder Bay ([https://services5.arcgis.com/h9xShea49ZANgOtx/arcgis/rest/services/Municipal_Address_Feature_Layer/FeatureServer/0 ArcGIS feature service]).
* '''Consumption path:''' fetched daily into a SQLite history by [https://github.com/skfd/ontario-address-changes ontario-address-changes] ([https://skfd.github.io/ontario-address-changes/thunder-bay/ change reports]); this import reads that read-only.

=== Licence ===
* '''Licence:''' [https://media-004-ca.cdn.govstack.com/thunderbay-002-ca/media/inmjquon/city-of-thunder-bay-open-data-licence.pdf The Corporation of the City of Thunder Bay Open Data Licence 1.0] (PDF; the City's old licence page is gone). Clause 5 requires the statement "Contains information licensed under the Open Data Licence - The Corporation of the City of Thunder Bay." Listed by the OSMF Licensing Working Group as compatible: [https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/OGL_Canada_and_local_variants OGL Canada and local variants], decided in the [https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Licensing_Working_Group/Minutes/2025-09-08 LWG minutes of 2025-09-08] (ticket #2025082810000396). Attribution goes in <code>addr:source</code> on each node and <code>source</code> on each changeset, and the City is listed on [[Contributors#Canada]].

=== Type and volume ===
* Points only: civic number, street, municipality (<code>THUNDER BAY</code> or <code>FWFN</code>), parcel id, property type. No unit field (14 units are written into the civic number; see Conflation), no postcodes, no ranges.

=== Freshness ===
* OSM side: Geofabrik Ontario extract, refreshed before each session. If more than 24 h pass between conflation and upload, re-conflate first.

== Tagging plan ==

All uploads are '''nodes'''.

{| class="wikitable"
! Tag !! From !! Notes
|-
| <code>addr:housenumber</code> || <code>ADDRESS</code> || The full civic number with its qualifier: <code>688B</code>, <code>963 1/2</code>. The City's integer column drops qualifiers on 338 rows, so it is not used.
|-
| <code>addr:street</code> || <code>ROOT</code> || The City publishes abbreviated capitals (<code>JAMES ST S</code>); expanded and title-cased on the way out: <code>James Street South</code>, <code>103rd Street</code>.
|-
| <code>addr:unit</code> || <code>ADDRESS</code> || Only on the 14 Caribou Crescent doors whose number the City writes as <code>270-1</code>.
|-
| <code>addr:source</code> || static || <code>City of Thunder Bay Open Data</code>
|-
| <code>addr:postcode</code> || OSM || Only copied from a same-address POI already in OSM. The City publishes no postcodes, and none are invented.
|}

'''Not written:''' <code>addr:city</code> (redundant inside the city; for FWFN, ask the Nation first), <code>addr:province</code>, <code>addr:country</code>, <code>addr:unit</code> except the 14 Caribou Crescent doors, ward, parcel id, property type.

